        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(google-oauth): cancel unread response body on non-ok HTTP responses",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes two response body leaks in Google OAuth project operations where HTTP error responses with unread bodies could keep the connection open until idle timeout.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nWhen the polling loop or onboardUser endpoint returns a non-ok HTTP status, the response body stream is not consumed before continuing or throwing. Unread response bodies can delay connection reuse and, in resource-constrained environments, contribute to file descriptor pressure.\n\nThe fix adds `response.body?.cancel()` before each `continue` and `throw`, matching the established pattern used across the codebase (openrouter/usage.ts, chutes/oauth.ts, lmstudio/models.fetch.ts, and others).\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior change. Connection reuse is slightly more efficient during Google OAuth project polling.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Real environment tested**: Local development environment\n\n**Exact steps or command run after this patch**: `npx tsx scripts/evidence-oauth.ts` — direct call to the `pollOperation`/`discoverProject` error path\n\n**After-fix evidence**:\n```\n  [RUN] Body cancel on non-ok response... Body cancelled: YES ✅ PASS ✅\n  [RUN] Double cancel is safe... Double cancel count: 2 — safe ✅ PASS ✅\n  [RUN] Null body is handled gracefully... Null body cancel: No error ✅ PASS ✅\n  [RUN] Cancel rejection doesn't mask original error... Cancel rejection: Suppressed by .catch ✅\n        Final error: \"Original error (status 401)\"\n        Original error preserved: YES ✅ PASS ✅\n\nResults: 4/4 passed\nCOMMAND_EXIT_CODE=0\n```\n\n**Observed result after the fix**:\n- `response.body?.cancel()` executes before throwing on non-ok responses\n- Double cancel is safe\n- Null body is handled gracefully\n- Cancel rejection doesn't mask the original error\n- Original error is preserved with correct status code\n\n**What was not tested**: Full Gateway integration with real Google OAuth. The above evidence covers the response body cancellation pattern that was added.",
